<title>USA: Range Systems Engineering wins US Navy contract.</title>
<headline>Range Systems Engineering wins US Navy contract.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-12-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. Navy said Monday it has awarded a $149 million contract to Range Systems Engineering Co to maintain and operate Atlantic Undersea Test and Evaluation Centers in the Bahamas and Florida.</p>
<p>It said 80 percent of the work will be done at the center on Andros Island in the Bahamas and 20 percent at the center at West Palm Beach, Fla.</p>
<p>The Burlington, Mass., company is to maintain and operate the centers until March 2002 under the contract, the Navy said.</p>
</text>
